 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Open–closed criterion",
 "statement": "A sheaf $\\mathcal F\\in\\shv{\\et X}$ is constructible if and only if\n$j^*\\mathcal F$ and $i^*\\mathcal F$ are constructible.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-smooth-purity/sk-prop-sf-cbc/prop-constructible-open-closed.md",
  "place": "node prop-constructible-open-closed, order 1537"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-constructible-constructible",
  "def-constructible-finite-locally-constant",
  "def-constructible-stratification"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "``Only if'' is [prop-constructible-pullback]. Conversely let\n$(\\kappa_l\\colon W_l\\to U)_{l<m}$ and $(\\lambda_k\\colon V_k\\to Z)_{k<n}$ be\nstratifications witnessing the constructibility of $j^*\\mathcal F$ and\n$i^*\\mathcal F$. The family of the $j\\circ\\kappa_l$ and the\n$i\\circ\\lambda_k$ is a stratification of $X$ with $m+n$ strata: each\ncomposite is an immersion; the images $j(U_l)$ are locally closed in $X$,\nbeing locally closed in the open $U$; the images $i(Z_k)$ are locally\nclosed in $X$, being locally closed in the closed $Z$; and the images are\npairwise disjoint and cover $X$ because the $U_l$ partition $U$, the $Z_k$\npartition $Z$, and $X=U\\sqcup Z$. Finally\n$(j\\circ\\kappa_l)^*\\mathcal F\\cong\\kappa_l^*j^*\\mathcal F$ and\n$(i\\circ\\lambda_k)^*\\mathcal F\\cong\\lambda_k^*i^*\\mathcal F$ are finite\nlocally constant by construction and [lemma-constructible-iso-invariance].",
   "uses": [
    "prop-constructible-pullback",
    "lemma-constructible-iso-invariance"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
